# Project Structure Guidelines

## Directory Organization
The project should follow a modular structure:

```
DhanKanya/
├── app/                    # Core application code
│   ├── api/                # API endpoints
│   ├── models/             # Data models
│   ├── services/           # Business logic services
│   └── utils/              # Utility functions
├── config/                 # Configuration files
├── tests/                  # Test files
│   ├── unit/               # Unit tests
│   └── integration/        # Integration tests
├── docs/                   # Documentation
├── scripts/                # Utility scripts
├── static/                 # Static files
├── .env.template           # Template for environment variables
├── requirements.txt        # Project dependencies
└── README.md               # Project documentation
```

## Main Files
- [README.md](mdc:README.md) - Project overview, installation, and usage
- [requirements.txt](mdc:requirements.txt) - Dependencies with specific versions

## Workflow Guidelines
- Organize code by feature and functionality
- Keep the repository root clean
- Group related modules in appropriately named packages
- Maintain separation of concerns between different modules
- Avoid circular dependencies between modules

## Configuration
- Store configuration in dedicated files
- Use environment variables for sensitive information
- Never commit secrets or credentials
- Include templates for configuration files

## Command Line Interface
- Implement CLI commands where appropriate
- Provide help text for all commands
- Use argument validation and clear error messages

## Static Files and Assets
- Organize assets by type
- Use appropriate formats for different types of assets
- Document the purpose and usage of key assets
